+- Blog, FAQ and changelog normal acceptance creates new entities; a revision cannot reuse that path. IngestDraftTarget identifies model associations, not the resulting formal blog/FAQ.
+- Full FAQ/changelog PUT treats translations as the complete final array and soft-deletes omitted locales. Revision acceptance requires a narrow transactional write.
+- Existing model-info acceptance invokes generation-related hooks and specialized overview receipts. Revision handling must avoid new generation while respecting content validation.
+- Read-only staging lookup confirmed Showcase 01M7RTXGZRFWQ77M85SN2VDREE pending with original media and FAQ 01M7RSYN4H4FHP9891TNPRVKAY accepted with the reported wording.
+- Original sites checkout has unrelated user changes. All edits stay in the feature worktree.
+
+Prisma concurrency reference consulted via Context7: conditional version match/update and affected-row checks prevent stale writes; row locks must be held inside the transaction that compares and writes. Installed ORM is 7.5.0, so existing project transaction APIs remain authoritative over newer-version examples.
