+# Rollout and staging acceptance
+
+Deploy the additive `20261120090000_draft_revisions` migration before the API code. Deploy API before distributing the companion CLI: the new CLI refuses to fall back to an unguarded write against older APIs.
+
+New acceptance mappings are recorded transactionally. Legacy accepted content is resolved only when identity/content associations can be verified; ambiguous targets require an explicit verified entity ID. Specialized overview-refill revisions remain on their existing source-proof workflow.
+
+## Staging checklist (after reviewed deployment)
+
+1. Read and save both pending Showcase snapshots: `01M7RTXMTT8R8EWNS5Q5Q404TM` and `01M7RTXGZRFWQ77M85SN2VDREE`.
+2. Apply approved title/introduce patches with their saved `updatedAt` using `--if-unmodified-since`, always `-e staging`.
+3. Read each draft back. Verify pending, same ID, expected copy, and identical input/prompt/artifact/media/hash/model/route/source. No jobs created.
+4. Read accepted FAQ `01M7RSYN4H4FHP9891TNPRVKAY` and its formal FAQ/locale. Save original publication timestamp, entity count, other translations and model visibility state.
+5. Propose the correction to say long images support only auto using a stable request ID. Confirm original accepted record and formal content remain unchanged; inspect trusted target association on the new pending draft.
+6. Replay the same operation and confirm the same draft ID. On a dedicated fixture, confirm changed payload with the same key fails, and stale versions fail atomically.
+7. After explicitly reviewing the correction, accept the staging revision. Verify same FAQ entity, corrected target locale, unchanged original accepted draft, publication timestamp, other locales, model/route visibility and no generation jobs.
+8. Exercise blog acceptance on isolated staging content: unchanged slug/entity ID, preserved other locales, and no duplicate article. Change the formal target between revise and accept to verify 409 leaves the revision pending.
+
+This implementation session submits review PRs. It does not deploy the migration/API, publish production content, accept the user's real staging FAQ, or claim this checklist has run. Local PostgreSQL integration evidence is recorded separately.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Rollback application code only before any new revision rows exist, keeping additive tables for audit. Once revision rows exist, do not expose them to older accept code: it lacks revision routing and would treat them as create-only drafts. Disable review mutations or roll forward the API fix. Do not drop trusted receipts/mappings while pending revision drafts exist.
